   "text": "Tenstorrent hits $6.2B valuation to scale open-weight AI chips \n\nIn Brief\n\nPosted:\n\n11:37 AM PDT \u00b7 October 19, 2026\n\nImage Credits:Tenstorrent\n\nTenstorrent, a chip startup focused on inference, has raised $1.5 billion at a $6.2 billion valuation. The round comes five months after the 10-year-old Nvidia challenger reportedly received acquisition interest from Intel and Qualcomm at valuations of as much as $5 billion.\n\nThe fresh round, which more than doubled Tenstorrent\u2019s valuation from the $2.6 billion it fetched in late 2024, was led by Trace Capital, a new firm launched by Quiet Capital co-founder Ben Mahdavi, and Innovation X. Other backers included Cadence Ventures, Eclipse, Fidelity, Sa",
